[001] Installation
________________________________________________________________________________

+------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                                                              |
|  $ kiss b librewolf                                                          |
|                                                                              |
+------------------------------------------------------------------------------+


--[002] Runtime Dependencies ----------------------------------------------------

  LibreWolf needs a few additional things to be fully functional. One is an
  icon theme and the other is a font. If you have already installed the fonts
  and icon theme of your choosing, this step can be skipped.

  +----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  |                                                                            |
  |   $ kiss b [hicolor-icon-theme|adwaita-icon-theme]                         |
  |   $ kiss b ttf-croscore                                                    |
  |                                                                            |
  +----------------------------------------------------------------------------+


[003] Setup
________________________________________________________________________________

As of Firefox 91. There is no need to set special environment variables to
enable Wayland support (in a Wayland only environment like ours). The browser
should start with no further configuration.

LibreWolf comes with a librewolf.cfg file that sets privacy-focused preferences
by default. This can be customized in /usr/lib/librewolf/librewolf.cfg.


[004] Usage
________________________________________________________________________________

Refer to the browser's help output and online documentation for further
information.


